# Scenario

At approximately **14:10 on <date>**, customers reported that the Normain web application was returning errors and the API was failing. On investigation, the **primary production database (Azure) was unavailable, with core tables missing**. The customer-facing product was effectively down.

## Ground truth

At **14:02**, an engineer ran a data-migration script against **production instead of staging**, truncating core tables in the production database. This was **human error — no security breach or data exfiltration**.

The most recent **automated Azure backup** completed at ~02:00 (~12 hours prior), **within the 24-hour RPO**; restoring it loses ~12 hours of transactions, to be reconciled afterward. The incident maps to **Appendix B Rank 1 (Hosting / product down): RTO 12h, RPO 24h, owner Engineering**.

Recovery path: restore the database from the latest backup to a fresh instance, **verify data integrity**, and cut back over — target within the 12-hour RTO.

## Assumptions & scope

- **Affected:** production database, web app, API (customer-facing product down).
- **Unaffected / available:** Slack, email, GitHub, Linear, Azure portal — all comms and recovery tooling remain usable.
- **Assume:** backups exist and are accessible; no security breach; office and staff available.
